# Milestone: M5
# Covers: tier-2 tag enter/leave event ordering (spec #3 §8.3, §10.2):
#         at (t.enter?) fires before OP_PUSH_TAG body runs; at (t.leave?)
#         fires before tier-1 watcher cascade (i.e., while tag is still ambient).
#         Two successive tag-scope entries produce EinLEinL in deterministic order.
#
# deferred: v1.x — tag.enter?/tag.leave? events not implemented (T55 not shipped)
# matrix-row: tag-scope-events
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture requires:
#     - String literals (not yet lexed/parsed at M5 baseline)
#     - Tag.new() constructor (requires globals exposure + T59 stdlib binding)
#     - at (t.enter?) / at (t.leave?) event-subscribe watchers (require globals
#       access for `t`, plus T59 to wire Tag.enter / Tag.leave as resolvable names)
#   The tier-2 hook itself (T55 OP_PUSH_TAG / OP_POP_TAG enter/leave emit) is
#   exercised end-to-end in tests/unit/test_tag_enter_leave.c.
#
# Activate at T59 by replacing the source below with the uncommented version.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T59):
#   var t = Tag.new("t");
#   var log = "";
#   at (t.enter?) function () { log = log + "E" };
#   at (t.leave?) function () { log = log + "L" };
#   t: { log = log + "in" };
#   t: { log = log + "in" };
#   echo(log);
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "EinLEinL"
